data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

.NET 11 / EF Core 11 **removes the sync-over-async opt-in** for the Cosmos DB provider entirely. In .NET 10 you could set:

```csharp
options.UseCosmos(...).ConfigureWarnings(w =>
    w.Ignore(CosmosEventId.SyncNotSupported));
```

In .NET 11, that workaround is gone. **Every synchronous call** against the Cosmos provider — `ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, `SaveChanges()` — throws an `InvalidOperationException` at runtime.

## All four methods are affected

| Sync (breaks) | Async (replacement) |
|---|---|
| `.ToList()` | `.ToListAsync()` |
| `.First(...)` | `.FirstAsync(...)` |
| `.Count()` | `.CountAsync()` |
| `.SaveChanges()` | `.SaveChangesAsync()` |

## Fix: convert to async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- `async Task<T>` return types replace synchronous returns
- Callers must be updated to `await` these methods (async propagates up the call stack)
- `Add()` stays synchronous — it only tracks the entity in memory; no I/O occurs until `SaveChangesAsync()`
